{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"agent_message","text":"Differential testing exposed one real compatibility gap: glibc’s `%d` path saturates at signed 64-bit limits before narrowing to C `int`, whereas my first parser wrapped every decimal digit directly into 32 bits. I’m correcting that behavior and switching from `read_to_end` to incremental scanning so the Rust program, like the C program, can finish after the 100th conversion without waiting for stdin EOF."}}
